    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier offensive anchor. With a score of 83.29, he benefits from a highly favorable matchup against Sugano (xERA 4.89) and a massive park factor boost (+14%). The combination of his high-leverage spot in the three-hole and a significant SP skill advantage makes him the clear foundation for our 5x5 production. We are also projecting significant upside from **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (76.57), who benefits from a favorable platoon split against the left-handed Cantillo. The synergy of the lineup\u2019s aggressive stacking against the weaker arms in today\u2019s rotation\u2014specifically the matchups for **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Coby Mayo** against Sugano\u2014should provide the best opportunity to push our R and RBI totals.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision occurred at the fringe of the starting rotation, where **Heliot Ramos** (49.25) narrowly missed the cut. While **Heliot Ramos** offers the high-end sprint speed we prioritize for our SB scarcity strategy, his score was suppressed by a poor matchup against Detmers (xERA 3.40). Ultimately, the algorithm prioritized the higher base efficiencies of **Luis Lara** and **Kyle Tucker**, despite their own challenging matchups against left-handed pitching. We are closely monitoring the status of **Andy Pages**, who remains sidelined on the IL, and we continue to watch for any late-breaking lineup shifts that could impact **Drake Baldwin** or **Sam Antonacci**, whose values are heavily leveraged on their confirmed spots at the top of the order.\n\nWhile we are optimized for maximum efficiency, we are keeping a close eye on the performance of **Kyle Tucker** and **Jackson Merrill** against left-handed starters. Both players face significant SP skill headwinds today, which tempered their final scores. While **Henry Bolte** (65.40) provides a strong floor thanks to his leadoff duties and a favorable park, the overall volatility of the day\u2019s pitching slate suggests we need to be ready to pivot our bench reserves like **Wade Meckler** if the early game weather reports or defensive changes alter the projections for our middle-of-the-pack starters. We are playing for volume and high-speed opportunity, ensuring that even in lower-scoring matchups, we maintain pressure on the stolen base category.",
